+# AutoVideoAI 7.0.79: Gemini Web send check, text cards that do not stop the set, Odia captions
+
+Update from 7.0.78 with `tools/update_v778_to_v779.py`. Code and documentation only. Saved jobs, outputs,
+browser profiles, music, characters and channel profiles are never copied, moved or deleted.
+
+## What was wrong (from the 7.0.78 dashboard log)
+
+1. **Gemini Web prompt was pasted but not sent.** The send step treated any click that did not raise as a
+   success. An unsent prompt then waited the full 300 seconds for an answer that never came, and the job
+   stopped with no error on the dashboard.
+2. **One bad text card stopped the whole set.** A card whose spoken anchor was too short or too long raised
+   "Choose a spoken anchor lasting 1.5-6 seconds" for every card, so the dashboard stayed at
+   "drafting timed cards" with a red box.
+3. **Odia captions could not use speech recognition.** Groq rejects Odia (HTTP 400) and the local Whisper
+   install fails in the user's environment, so the caption step ended in fallbacks.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Send is verified.** After the click, the composer is read. If the prompt is still there, Enter is pressed
+  once. If it is still there, the run fails at once with a clear Gemini Web message, instead of waiting 300 s.
+  An unreadable composer is never treated as sent, unless Gemini shows it is generating an answer.
+- **Text cards are dropped one at a time.** An unusable card is removed and its reason is recorded; the rest of
+  the set is kept. A long spoken phrase is clamped to 6 seconds instead of rejected. Overlapping cards keep the
+  earlier one. If the cards cover too much of the video, the longest are trimmed.
+- **Wrong-script cards are dropped in Odia and Hindi editions.** Card copy in the wrong script is removed and
+  reported. If every card is in the wrong script and the first answer came back quickly (under 90 s), the
+  draft is requested once more with a correction. A slow answer is not asked for again.
+- **Saved results that lost every card are retried.** A saved text-card result with no cards left and a
+  recorded drop reason is not reused on the next run.
+- **Odia captions skip speech recognition in auto mode.** Groq and local Whisper are not called for Odia; the
+  timing is estimated from the reviewed script. An explicit Groq or local choice for Odia fails with a clear
+  message instead of a silent fallback.
+
+## Limits, stated plainly
+
+- Odia caption timing is **estimated, not measured**. The 2-3 second transcript lag reported for Odia is not
+  confirmed fixed by this release. The Odia voice file from the user's job has not been reviewed yet.
+- Dropped text cards are shown in the job's `speech_cards.json` under `dropped_cards` and printed in the log.
+  They are not yet shown in the dashboard.
+
+## Tests
+
+- `tests/test_v779_submit_cards_timing.py`: 17 tests, all passing. On the 7.0.78 code 16 of them fail (the one
+  that passes is the English Groq check, which is expected), so they catch the original bugs.
+- Eight older tests were updated to the new behaviour: four anchor checks in `test_v765`, one single-card check
+  in `test_v774`, the Odia refusal in `test_v778` (now a drop with a reason), and two Gemini fake-page checks in
+  `test_v576` (the fake send step now takes the prompt).
+- Known failures that already fail on the untouched 7.0.78 code (not caused by this release): 9 in
+  `test_card_typography`, 2 in `test_presentation_dashboard`, 2 in `test_v580_production`, 1 in
+  `test_v731_dashboard_uploads`, 2 in `test_v733_publication_review`, 1 in `test_v735_bounded_upload`,
+  1 in `test_v753_workflow`, 4 in `test_v758_uploads_picker`. These are not part of the Odia work.
+- The full suite needs `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe` on the PATH (some tests render short clips); without them the run is not valid.
+
+## Updating from 7.0.78
+
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.79/tools/update_v778_to_v779.py .            # dry run
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.79/tools/update_v778_to_v779.py . --apply    # install
+
+Stop the dashboard first and restart it afterwards. From 7.0.77, first run the 7.0.78 updater from the 7.0.78 zip
+folder, as the updater's message says. The updater refuses to replace a file you have changed locally.
